03629cam a2200505 i in0000018514320250403134754.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||240805s2024    si a    ob    000 0 eng d  a9789819737215q(electronic bk.)  a9819737214q(electronic bk.)  z9789819737208  z98197372067 a10.1007/978-981-97-3721-52doi  aspon1450874097  a(OCoLC-M)1450874097  aYDXbengerdaepncYDXdGW5XEdOCLCOdEBLCPdCStdUtOrBLW  aMAIN 4aTL79004a629.401/51223/eng/202408071 aYuan, Jianping,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8416196610aJet transport technique :btheory and application /cJianping Yuan, Jianlin Chen, Chen Gao, Chuan Ma, Josep J. Masdemont, Gerard Gómez 1aSingapore :bSpringer ;aBeijing :bScience Press,c[2024] 4c©2024  a1 online resource (ix, 180 pages) :billustrations (chiefly color)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references  aThis book focuses on the Jet Transport (JT) technique and gives a systematic introduction on its theory development, algorithm implementation, and in particular, the applications in the field of astronautics including uncertainty propagation, filtering, as well as guidance and control. It features on the combination of mathematical theory and engineering applications, making the technique to be understood and mastered straightforwardly. Moreover, the JT-based methods proposed in the book offer a new and ingenious way to some classical problems. Given its breadth of coverage, the book offers a valuable reference guide for researchers and engineers interested in the JT methodology including theory and applications0 aIntroduction -- The Implementation of Jet Transport Software -- Analysis of Orbit Uncertainty Propagation Using Jet Transport -- Jet Transport Application to Particle Filter for Attitude Estimation of Tumbling Space Objects -- Jet Transport based High Order Kalman Filter for Joint Orbit and Parameter Estimation -- Autonomous Orbit Determination and Fault tolerant Designs Using Jet Transport -- Jet Transport based Adaptive Order switching Filter -- Low thrust Station Keeping at Libration Point Orbits Using Jet Transport0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed August 7, 2024) 0aAstronauticsxMathematics. 6aAstronautiquexMathématiques.1 aChen, Jianlin,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20200391451 aGao, Chen,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780575861 aMa, Chuan,eauthor.1 aMasdemont, Josep J.,eauthor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJjdfpJfwp4CB3Y96xkJjC0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20031082981 aGómez, G.q(Gerard),eauthor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjyDK6grq4g9WJmRBPqMCP0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n0001377908iPrint version:z9819737206z9789819737208w(OCoLC)143320127140zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://link.springer.com/10.1007/978-981-97-3721-5xWMSySpringerLinkxProvider: SpringerxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxsp4xspon1450874097  aeLoaderRecord xsp4  a92bSTFffi0000155b-5a17-4813-8dc3-b65f4e1a07c5s40bfa813-fbb7-485e-b270-5931118caebb02628njm a22005417i in0000029813520250403134754.0m        h        sz zunnnnnuneucr nnannnuuuuu250225s2024    xx uunn o         n zxx d0 aITLF522092320 aITLF522092330 aITLF522092340 aITLF522092350 aITLF522092360 aITLF5220923702aDV-C00605bDa Vinci Classics  anmon1501592283  a(OCoLC)1501592283  aNAXOSbengerdaepncNAXOSdOCLCOdCstdUtOrBLW1 aArena, Michele,ecomposer,eperformer.10aChamber music.kSelections10aConvergence(s) :bcontemporary music for electronics and instruments /cMichele Arena, Leo Cicala 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bDa Vinci Classics,c[2024]  a1 online resource (1 audio file)  a004643  aperformed musicbprm2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  adigital2rdatr  aaudio file2rdaft0 aMichele Arena, Leo Cicala, electronics ; with various other soloists0 aRapsodia (5:29) -- Immagini riflesse (7:53) -- Ritratto di un viaggiatore solitario (9:20) -- Osiris (8:13) -- Dàidalos (6:24) -- Moto interiore (9:24) 0aChamber music.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85022422 6aMusique de chambre.0(CaQQLa)201-00460871 aCicala, Leo,ecomposer,eperformer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20191803941https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjrYwj9mQgQj3xrw9QBhXm12iContainer of (work):aCicala, Leo.tChamber music.kSelections.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tRapsodia,minstrumental ensemble.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tImmagini riflesse.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tRitratto di un viaggiatore solitario.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tOsiris.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tDàidalos.12iContainer of (work):aArena, Michele.tMoto interiore.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttp://stanford.naxosmusiclibrary.com/catalogue/item.asp?cid=DV-C00605yNaxos Music LibraryxProvider: NaxosxCollection: Naxos Music LibraryxsubscribedxeLoaderURLxnm4xnmon1501592283  aeLoaderRecordxum4  aC0bNAXOSffi00007684-171c-4b1e-9e09-e360fd034fa1s97807537-963c-4f7d-89f5-68b06957961902630cam a2200469 i in0000023133820250403134754.0240322t20242024enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2024013189  a9781800504936qhardcover  a1800504934qhardcover  a9781800504943qpaperback  a1800504942qpaperback  z9781800504950qelectronic book  z9781800505865qelectronic book 9agls20960848  a(OCoLC)1427940777  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdYDXdUtOrBLW  apcc00aBT825b.R45 202400a236/.1223/eng/2024040200aReligion, death and the senses /cedited by Christina Welch and Jasmine Hazel Shadrack 1aSheffield, South Yorkshire ;aBristol, CT :bEquinox Publishing, Ltd,c2024 4c©2024  axvi, 288 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aReligion and the senses  aIncludes bibliographical references and index  a"The uniqueness of this collection lies in two areas, firstly its deep engagement with a range of physical and socio-cultural sensual responses to death and dying, and secondly, through its contributors who are drawn from a wide spectrum of professional, practical, and theoretical expertise and scholarship in fields which continue to redefine our understanding of mortality"--cProvided by publisher 0aDeathxReligious aspectsxChristianity.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85036098 6aMortxAspect religieuxxChristianisme.1 aWelch, Christina,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20180839721 aShadrack, Jasmine Hazel,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no202113547808iOnline version:tReligion, death and the sensesdSheffield, South Yorkshire ; Bristol, CT : Equinox Publishing, Ltd, 2024z9781800504950w(DLC)  2024013190 0aReligion and the senses.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2019061661  aGOBI  aSAL3 StacksbTHOMASC-SULc90100515416dbooke100.00fJCg325028kUSDm0.00q1rCan circulatetPurchaseuVendor order reference numbervYANKEE-SUL  aSAL3 StacksbTHOMASC-SULc90100515416dbooke81.00fJCg325028h243333kUSDm0.00q1rCan circulatetPurchaseuVendor order reference numbervYANKEE-SUL  a36105232773866ffsa3aa6b65-fd2c-47d2-874a-fbd0d04f8db9i00016bb4-b76c-47a5-8b6e-23a0e0590b5104265nam a2200553ui in0000030437220250403134754.0a||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu240904s2024||||xx ||||go|||||||| u|eng|d  als175342  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aambivalent work*s: queer perspectives and art history 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bDiaphanes,c2024  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"ambivalent work*s presents case studies, close- and against-the-grain readings of art works across different media and geographies, conversations on the epistemological and methodological frameworks of a queerly-informed art history, and artistic contributions. Together they revisit central aspects such as visibility, failure, transgression and subversion in recent art production while at the same time providing valuable links for transhistorical explorations. The book highlights queerness in visual and material culture with regard to the specific conditions of the making and experience of art in different cultural, sociopolitical, and historical contexts. Making a case for polyvalence and simultaneity, ambivalent work*s demonstrates how intersectional approaches extend the examination of queer capacities in art and art history beyond issues related solely to sexuality and gender. Scholarly and artistic articulations equally push the boundaries of the academic field of art history while giving shape to an (im)possible project of a "queer art history.""--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY10aArt criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500798910aArtxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500748810aSexual minority culture.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh201910354217aArt criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008154920http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81549217aArt History.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081539617aSexual minority culture.2fast0(OCoLC)fst020108600http://id.worldcat.org/fast/2010860 7aDiscursive works.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089 7aEssay Collection.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014240321 aBerndt, Daniel,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20170572911 aDoyle, Jennifer,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n950715621 aGajowy, Aleksandra,econtributor.1 aGetsy, David J.,econtributor.1 aHuber, Susanne,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n960333881 aKöppert, Katrin,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20130225091 aLiclair, Christian,eeditor,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20210632041 aLorenz, Renate,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20090626961 aMcGovern, Fiona,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20141446851 aMergenthaler, Diyi,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20220625351 aOdahara, Lucas,econtributor.1 aOnat, Rena,econtributor.1 aPaul, Barbara,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n852379661 aSepahvand, Ashkan,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20150688792 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/ambivalent-works-queer-perspectives-and-art-history/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls17534242uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Ambivalent-Works-480x778.pngzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi0003b975-5b67-43e9-bd6c-267cb3bd282fs299cbc1a-8b01-4595-b4f5-f6d4f41ad46702574nam a22002418i 4500001001400000005001700014006001900031007001500050008004100065020001800106024004500124035001800169040002700187110010700214245019500321260003600516300001000552520144700562650002802009856019302037910002302230999007902253in0000022566420250403134754.0a     o  d i      cr || |||a|n||240701s2021    |||     o    i|0| 0 eng d  a97892647261237 ahttps://doi.org/10.1787/0132c06d-en2doi  aoi0132c06d-en  aFR-PaOECdCStdUtOrBLW2 aOrganisation for Economic Co-operation and Development.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7904535410aG20/OECD-INFE Report on Supporting Financial Resilience and Transformation through Digital Financial Literacyh[electronic resource] /cOrganisation for Economic Co-operation and Development  aParis :bOECD Publishing,c2021  a42 p.3 aThis report discusses the concept of financial resilience and its relationship with financial inclusion, financial literacy and financial well-being. It offers a wide range of case studies looking at the role of digital financial education initiatives addressing financial resilience and vulnerability. It proposes set of effective approaches describing how the digital financial education programmes can support individual financial resilience and long-term well-being. The effective approaches complement the provisions of the OECD Council Recommendation on Financial Literacy, which was welcomed by G20 Finance Ministers and Central Bank Governors on 9-10 July 2021. The effective approaches and lessons learnt presented in this report have provided input for the development of the G20 Menu of Policy Options for digital financial literacy and financial consumer and MSME protection "Enhancing digital financial inclusion beyond the COVID-19 crisis" developed by the GPFI. This report was prepared in support of the agenda of the G20 Global Partnership on Financial Inclusion (GPFI) under the G20 Italy Presidency 2021, as well as part of the work of the OECD International Network on Financial Education (OECD/INFE). The report reflects inputs and guidance from GPFI member countries, Implementing Partners, Affiliated Partners and other key stakeholders, and particularly members of the OECD/INFE, via an extensive consultation process 4aFinance and Investment.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://doi.org/10.1787/0132c06d-enyOECD iLibraryxProvider: OECD PublishingxCollection: OECD iLibraryxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxoi4xoi0132c06d-en  aeLoaderRecordxoi4ffi0006d4e7-5f5c-4dc3-b6ee-4b7f8510c347sdc275a75-534d-41ee-a3b0-a3b1610a696403957nam a22005053i in0000029256720250403134754.0m     o  d  ||||||cr unu||||||||240318s2024    sz |    o    |||| 0|eng d  z9783031505027  a9783031505034 (online)  a(EBZ)ebs104773227e  dEBZdUtOrBLW  amsc 4aS5900 aFrontier Studies in Soil Science.10aFrontier Studies in Soil Science /cedited by Avelino Núñez-Delgado  a1st ed. 2024 1aCham :bSpringer International Publishing :bImprint: Springer,c2024  ap. ;ccm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aFrontier Studies in Soil Science,x3004-98730 aIntroduction chapter -- Antibiotics as emerging pollutants of soil ecosystems -- Rare Earths in Soils -- Impact of agricultural wastes on environment and possible management strategies -- Organic carbon management and the relations with climate change -- Agricultural soil management impacts on soil microbial communities -- Antibiotics, other emerging pollutants, and pathogenic microorganisms in raw and treated sewage sludge reaching soils -- Remediation of PTEs contaminated soils by washing treatment with biodegradable reagents -- Natural barriers to antibiotic entry into the trophic chain: some examples of the role of soils and by-products -- Salt-Affected Soils -- Beyond the obvious: exploring peat vibrational spectroscopy (FTIR-ATR) data using principal component analysis on transposed data matrix (tPCA), Store Mosse bog (Sweden) -- Application of biochar in agricultural soil green remediation and sustainable development -- Frontier Studies in Soil Science: A Conclusions Chapter  aThis is the first book where top researchers focus on presenting new research proposals in soil science. All the authors contributing to the book have a solid background and experience in specific fields of soil science, allowing them to propose the critical lines of future development in their respective and particular paths of cut-edge investigation. The primary audiences for the work are scientists/researchers working in these fields, as well as students interested in the views from top scientists on recent and future trends in the area, and all those in the overall society desiring to be aware of possible pathways for the future of soil science 0aSoil science.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85124376 0aEcology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85040752 0aGeochemistry.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8505396010aSoil science.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8512437620aEnvironmental sciences.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9200404820aGeochemistry.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh850539601 aNúñez Delgado, Avelino,eeditor.4edt4http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/relators/edt0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n950999792 aSpringerLink (Online service)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20050467560 tSpringer Earth and Environmental Science eBooks 2024 English/International dSpringer Nature08iPrinted edition:z978303150502708iPrinted edition:z978303150504108iPrinted edition:z97830315050581 tFrontier Studies in Soil Science 0aFrontier Studies in Soil Science.403Full text available: 2024.zAvailable in Springer Earth and Environmental Science eBooks 2024 English/International.uhttps://link.springer.com/10.1007/978-3-031-50503-4  aFrontier%20Studies%20in%20Soil%20Science  aBookffi00081d8c-1814-496c-9d0a-d2fd71522a0dsf690491a-e320-4e33-9ade-32d7a7f9ea0a01530cam a2200361 i in0000025795620250403134754.0241212t20242024ug       b    000 0 fre c  a9789913642996  a991364299X 9aHogarth63861929004535  a(OCoLC)on1478262264  a(OCoLC)1478262264  aIULbengerdacIULdSTFdUtOrBLW  apcc  af-cg--- 4aDT650.M42bK394 20241 aKayembe Pamfulu, Jean-Marie Vianney,d1969-eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no202413880610aComprendre la culture du peuple Ambala de Luiza au Kasaï-Central en République Démocratique du Congo /cJean-Marie Vianney Kayembe Pamfulu 1aKampala :bBlessing Publishers,c[2024] 4c©2024  axii, 72 pages ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 69-70) 0aMbala (African people)zCongo (Democratic Republic)zLuiza (Territory)xSocial life and customs. 0aLuiza (Congo : Territory)xSocial life and customs.  aHogarth  hHELD BY STF - 1 OTHER HOLDINGS  aSAL3 StacksbLINDER-SULcHOGARTH795346dbookfkafkUSDm15.75q1rCan circulatetApproval planuVendor internal numbervHOGARTH-9999-SUL  aZ0bSTFffs81d0fea6-981d-4df9-ae06-4a1b299c6a5di000ae9be-67d0-4749-b1e7-ab3e01faf65505259nab a2200769ui in0000030216720250403134754.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu240411s2021||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als162684  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aMeta-Futures 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bDruštvo Galerija Boks,c2021  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aŠum ;v17  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"A meta-move is the diagonalization of the existing move set. A play outside the existing frame of action that has run its course by solving problems so efficiently that it hasn't realized these problems don't exist anymore. A move that manages to break the "path dependency" haunting all cultures (or software adaptations). Rather than blindly optimizing the current systemic trajectories and entrusting our hopes to the supposedly alien feedback dynamics outside the Human, it is possible to find a "meta-game of every other game" and unlock a new abstract space from within: from inside the game that simply has to be played in a better way (and is searching for new meta-players). If this doesn't resonate with the deadlock of Modernity (as a historical event and not periodization before post-modernity), nothing will. Even if we've slowly come to realise that we live in a process reality, we haven't been able to update this fact into a coherent set of parameters, into a systemic framework that will push us towards a new attractor. That will enable us to find a new plethora and save us from within. Figures like Benjamin Bratton are right to point out that our time calls for a "radically different sort of philosophy" that will once and for all break with the fetishes of post-modernity and/or the confusions surrounding the Human. That will see itself in the same way the crow sees the sparrow..."--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aCritical theory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800245610aEcology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8504075210aHistorical materialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506119610aNeurosciences--Philosophy.10aPhilosophy.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8510084910aPolitical science.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8510444017aCritical theory.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008836900http://id.worldcat.org/fast/88369017aEcology.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009014760http://id.worldcat.org/fast/90147617aHistorical materialism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009581410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/95814117aNeurosciences.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010365160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/103650917aPhilosophy.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010607770http://id.worldcat.org/fast/106077717aPolitical science.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010697810http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1069781 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/14116411 aCaron, J.-P.,econtributor.1 aGarcía, Bosco,econtributor.1 aGriško, Miroslav,econtributor.1 aGuidi, Tiago,econtributor.1 aHillani, Allan M.,econtributor.1 aMillie, J.,econtributor.1 aNaderi, Reza,econtributor.1 aPedroso, Rafael,econtributor.1 aPogačar, Tjaša,eeditor.1 aProsen, Timotej,econtributor.1 aRatcliffe, Jonathan,econtributor.1 aSaldanha, Rafael,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20230333681 aShulkin, Yasha,econtributor.1 aSilveira, Maikel da,econtributor.1 aŠkufca, Andrej,eeditor.1 aŠuštar, Miha,eproofreader.1 aTroha, Tisa,eeditor,econtributor.